# Keep the host's build tree out of the image.
#
# Not a size optimisation. CMakeCache.txt records the absolute path it was
# generated in, so a host build/ copied into /src makes the container's
# configure fail outright:
#
#   CMake Error: The current CMakeCache.txt directory /src/build/CMakeCache.txt
#   is different than the directory /home/<user>/.../build where CMakeCache.txt
#   was created.
#
# That is a confusing failure to hit from a clean checkout, because it depends
# on whether someone happened to run cmake on the host first.
build/
build-*/

.git/
.github/
*.o
*.so
*.so.*
compile_commands.json

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
